feat(lpa-horizon): log the pre-registered outcome and add two post hoc checks

Records the outcome of the pre-registered run (LS6 job 3600628, verdict
PARTIAL_PERSISTENCE) in the readout, then declares two analyses designed
after that outcome was read, before either is run on real data:

  P1  same Cox model stratified on the seven combinations of qualifying
      condition (prior infarction, ischaemic stroke, peripheral disease),
      with every endpoint within each condition
  P2  LDL-C calibration: the Lp(a) estimate expressed as an equivalent
      LDL-C difference (Fieller interval) and as the trial hazard ratio
      it predicts under the CTT rate ratio of 0.78 per 1 mmol/L

lpa_horizon_posthoc.R sources the pre-registered script unchanged (the
SLURM wrapper refuses to run if its md5 differs) and carries its own
synthetic self-test (LS6 job 3600659, 12 checks). Neither check can
change the verdict of record.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 


